;; Generic explicit work-state boundary for tail-recursive expansion.
;; These are primitive obligations, not opaque stack-building shortcuts.
;;
;; begin-traversal creates one pending root and no discoveries. take-pending
;; returns stable first work and remaining state. discovered-occurrence? is
;; support-sensitive and false only with complete membership. Registration is
;; atomic and precedes expansions. Expansion positions are stable and retain
;; their source-node anchors; incomplete tails
;; remain pending. finish-traversal completes only with complete membership and
;; no work. None of these operations acquires or executes source.
;; Implementations are versioned definitions in the traversal implementation
;; slot. This file declares the contract; hierarchy.lain owns their composition.
